 pilolo:['Chase','Search & race','PILOLO! RACE HOME.','A leader hides three sticks in nine baskets. On the call, search a basket with Space. Find one stick and race home before the two rival seekers. Three rounds; first home wins each round.'],
 stay:['Street','Planted-foot return','STAY SHOULD CATCH YOU THERE.','Move until the call, then press Stay. Keep your feet planted and return the incoming ball: E for a low kick, Q for a high header. Five throws. This implements a documented planted-foot variant; local rules differ.'],
 alikoto:['Skill','Pen-cap flip','LAND IT ON THE BASE.','Flip an improvised pen-cover and metal-cap spinner. Hold Palm strike to set force, then release. E adjusts a preset force. A point depends on its actual upright landing. Five attempts; points replace forfeits.'],
 tumatu:['Rhythm','Out-and-back hopscotch','ONE FOOT. INSIDE THE LINES.','Hop through the chalk squares and back, skipping square 4 with its marker. Tap a square to aim. Hold Hop longer for distance, especially the gap. Walking is disabled; land inside the chalk boundary.'],
 oware:['Boards','CPU or local 2-player','OWARE — ABAPA','Sow from a house on your side. Feed an empty opponent; captures cannot empty the opposing side. First to 25 seeds wins. Computer opponent by default; choose local two-player in settings. Threefold repetition is a digital end convention.'],
 dame:['Boards','CPU or local 2-player','DAME AT THE CORNER','Ghana-inspired 10×10: 20 pieces, mandatory backward captures, flying kings and complete capture chains. Captured pieces block until the chain ends; promotion is deferred. This declared variant loses at one remaining piece and draws after 80 quiet moves.'],
 ludo:['Boards','CPU or local 2-player','BRING ALL FOUR HOME','Four tokens each. Six to enter and roll again; exact roll to finish. Start squares are safe. This classic preset has no blockades, capture bonus or three-sixes penalty. Computer opponent by default; local two-player in settings.'],
 counters:['Street','CPU or local 2-player','BOTTLE TOPS. REAL TOUCH.','Choose a cap and aim at the pebble ball. Hold Flick to control force. E changes cap. First to three goals, or highest score after 24 flicks. Play against the computer or select local two-player in settings.'],
 kpitinge:['Skill','Weighted-peg toss','PLANT THE POINT.','Aim left/right and release the weighted practice peg near vertical. Its actual flight, landing location and orientation decide whether it plants in the sand mound. Five attempts; points replace forfeits.'],
 alasa:['Skill','Seed-flick duel','FIVE SEEDS EACH.','Take turns with the computer flicking star-apple-shaped seeds into a small hole. Aim left/right or tap the ground. Hold Flick to set force; E changes the preset. Only seeds sunk count. Five seeds each.'],
 numbers:['Compound','Quick-response circle','YOUR TURN. THINK QUICK.','Players name prime numbers in turn. Choose a prime before the response window closes. Wrong or late answers leave the circle. Eight turns get progressively quicker; the time windows and numeric choices are digital conventions.'],
 chempe:['Compound','Food-holder & claimant','REMEMBER WHO CALLS WHAT.','Alternate roles. When food appears, the food-holder calls “No Chem pe!” to keep the exemption; the claimant calls “Chempε!” first to request equal sharing. Six reflex exchanges. The timing contest is an optional arcade adaptation.'],
 pempenaa:['Rhythm','Leg-counting game','FOLLOW THE PHRASE.','Four seated players extend both legs. The count moves across the remaining legs. At phrase-end, the selected leg folds. When your leg is selected, choose left or right. The first with both legs folded ranks first. Phrase lengths are an arcade convention.'],
 mbobagor:['Rhythm','Shared stone rhythm','ONE STONE FOR EACH PLAYER.','Six seated players each pass a stone anticlockwise on the shared clap. Press Pass on the beat. Missing a transfer leaves an extra stone in your pile. Sixteen passes wins; three piled stones end this arcade round.'],
 tyre:['Skill','Runner & tyre','PUSH. STEER. BALANCE.','Run behind a tyre and guide it with a stick through eight gates. Push gives a short burst; Sprint keeps pace. Avoid crates. Gate order and the 75-second time trial are arcade additions.'],
 pretend:['Compound','Open-ended role play','LIFE IN THE COMPOUND','Carry the basket, water and toy meal to their stations. There is no failing timer. These optional household tasks are an interpretation of open-ended Maame ne Paapa play.'],
 pampanaa:['Chase','Cover & sight lines','SEE THEM BEFORE THEY SEE YOU.','Move around cover, face a nearby rival and Tag. Rivals patrol and can spot you with a clear line of sight. Tag five before losing three chances. This solo scoring format adapts the documented team hide-and-spot game.']
